>> title: BLT
>> category: Sandwiches & Rolls
>> tags: bacon, tomato, lettuce, sandwich, lunch
>> counters: Diner
>> aka: BLT, bacon lettuce and tomato, bacon lettuce tomato sandwich, bacon sandwich
>> servings: 2
>> time: 20 min
>> step.1: render 10 min, from a cold pan
>> step.2: toast the four slices 2 min
>> step.3: spread both inside faces
>> step.4: salt the tomato, layer, cut once

Fry @thick-cut bacon{6%slices} laid in a cold #skillet{} brought slowly to medium ~fry{10%min}, turning once. A cold start renders the fat out before the meat seizes, which is what gives flat crisp strips instead of curled ones with raw white seams.

Toast @white sandwich bread{4%slices} ~toast{2%min}, to firm rather than dark.

Spread @mayonnaise{3%Tbs}(45 mL) over both inside faces of @&(~1)toast{}. Both faces, not one: the mayonnaise is waterproofing as much as seasoning, and the tomato is about to sit on it.

Layer @&(~3)bacon{}, @beefsteak tomato{1%large}(in 1/4-in slices), @iceberg lettuce{4%leaves}(cold and dry), @kosher salt{1/4%tsp} and @black pepper{1/4%tsp} onto @&(~1)dressed toast{}, and cut it once on the diagonal. Salt the tomato slices on a plate and let them drip for a minute before they go on — an unsalted tomato tastes of nothing and a salted one that goes straight on floods the toast.
